---
import WorkbenchLayout from "../../../layouts/WorkbenchLayout.astro";
---

<WorkbenchLayout
  title="Workbench Terms | PENGO Workbench"
  description="Terms for using the PENGO Workbench reference library."
  url="https://pengosystems.com/workbench/terms/"
  active="terms"
  breadcrumb="Workbench Terms"
>
  <article class="wb-content wb-template">
    <p class="wb-type-label">Terms</p>
    <h1>Workbench Terms</h1>
    <p class="wb-lede">
      Terms for using the PENGO Workbench public reference library.
    </p>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>Reference Material</h2>
      <p>
        PENGO Workbench is a public reference library for inspecting AI-facing failure
        surfaces, structural Patterns, diagnostic Lenses, AI-Adjacent Issues, and Check Input outputs.
      </p>
      <p>
        Workbench material is provided for reference, education, analysis, and discussion.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>Not Professional Advice</h2>
      <p>
        Workbench material is not legal, medical, financial, security, compliance,
        procurement, or operational advice.
      </p>
      <p>
        Do not rely on Workbench pages as the sole basis for decisions that require
        professional judgment, formal review, or organizational approval.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>No Guarantee of Fit</h2>
      <p>
        Workbench references may help identify related structures, but they may not fit
        every system, workflow, model, tool, prompt, organization, or use case.
      </p>
      <p>
        You are responsible for deciding whether a Workbench reference applies to your context.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>User Responsibility</h2>
      <p>
        You are responsible for how you interpret, reuse, cite, or apply Workbench material,
        including any decisions made from AI outputs, mapped results, or related pages.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</WorkbenchLayout>
